\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  Shooting Followed Years of Demonization\b0\par\par\uc2 By Apoorva Mandavilli \par \uc2 1,247 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 August 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees expressed horror at a shooting at the agency's headquarters, and some said they viewed it as part of a pattern of threats and assaults on health workers.\par \par \uc2 The day after a lone gunman opened fire on the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 , killing a police officer and shattering windows across the agency's campus, employees were reeling from shock, fear and rage.\par \par \uc2 ''We're mad this has happened,'' Dr. \uc2 Debra Houry\uc2 , the \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2 's chief medical officer, said in a large group call Saturday morning with Susan Monarez, the agency's newly confirmed director, who tried to reassure them. Another employee on the call, a recording of which was obtained by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 , asked Dr. Monarez: ''Are you able to speak to the misinformation, the disinformation that caused this issue? And what your plan forward is to ensure this doesn't happen again?''\par \par \uc2 The investigation into the shooting and the gunman's potential motives was still in early stages on Saturday. But law enforcement officials said that the suspect identified in the shooting had become fixated with the coronavirus vaccine, believing that it was the cause of his physical ailments.\par \par \uc2 Inside the \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2 , the shooting was viewed as part of a pattern in which health workers have been targets of political, verbal and physical assaults on them and their workplaces.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Demetre Daskalakis, the director of the \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2 's respiratory diseases division, told Dr. Monarez on the call that employees wanted to see a plan for their safety and an acknowledgment that the attack was not just ''a shooting that just happened across the street with some stray bullets.''\par \par \uc2 Dr. Daskalakis was not in his office when its windows were pierced by one of the gunman's bullets.\par \par \uc2 Many Americans, and even some top federal health officials in the Trump administration, have blamed the \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  for lockdowns, school closings and vaccine mandates, even when some of those decisions were made by state and local governments, or businesses.\par \par \uc2 ''I am heartbroken, angry and somehow not surprised,'' said Dr. Anne Zink, a former president of the \uc2 Association of State and Territorial Health Officials\uc2  who served as Alaska's chief medical officer until last year.\par \par \uc2 Threats against her have increased even though she is no longer a government official, she said.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  spoke with or texted a dozen \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  scientists on Saturday, who discussed the shooting on the condition of anonymity for fear of retaliation. They described being terrified as bullets shattered the glass windows, and some recounted the chilling sight of casings littered in front of the \uc2 C.D.C.\par \par \uc2 In interviews, the employees conveyed sadness about the police officer who had died trying to keep them safe, and a feeling of betrayal and devastation at being demonized while working to improve Americans' health.\par \par \uc2 The sound of rapid gunfire started around 4:50 p.m. on Friday. One scientist who evaluates Covid vaccines had just stepped out of her building to walk to her car. As she headed to pick up her infant daughter from day care, shots rang out over her right shoulder, she said. She turned around, ran back inside and called security to confirm what was happening.\par \par \uc2 ''C.D.C. SHELTER IN PLACE. GUNMAN AT EMORY POINT,'' she wrote to friends and colleagues in a group chat at 4:57 p.m. (The agency did not send out its alert to employees until 5:13 p.m.)\par \par \uc2 The employee and three others barricaded themselves in an office, moving two loaded bookshelves against the door. She put a sticky note over the motion sensor for the light switch and laid flat on the floor for hours, before a SWAT team arrived to clear the floor.\par \par \uc2 She finally made it home to her husband and two young children around midnight. In a text message sent at 3:11 a.m., she said she was still awake, too traumatized to sleep.\par \par \uc2 At least four buildings were damaged by bullets, Dr. Monarez said in a statement Friday night. Photos shared by workers revealed glass windows shattered by bullet holes. One showed as many as 18 bullet holes in a single building.\par \par \uc2 One of the buildings included a containment lab of the highest biosecurity level, but under tight security and with reinforced walls. It was not hit in the attack. The \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  studies some of the most dangerous pathogens in the world, including Ebola and Marburg viruses and the bacteria that cause anthrax.\par \par \uc2 Health Secretary \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2 , who oversees the \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2 , did not make a statement on Friday. Late Saturday morning, more than 30 minutes after posting photos of himself fishing on social media, Mr. Kennedy posted condolences on his official X account and pledged to support \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  employees.\par \par \uc2 In an email sent later in the day to the entire \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , including the \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2 , Mr. Kennedy wrote: ''This is a reminder of the very human challenges public servants sometimes face -- even in places dedicated to healing and progress. But it also reinforces the importance of the work you do every day.''\par \par \uc2 On the Saturday morning \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  call, an employee asked Dr. Monarez twice if she had spoken to Mr. Kennedy. Both times Dr. Monarez replied that she had been in touch with the ''office of the secretary.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kennedy has previously called the \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  a ''cesspool of corruption'' and a fascist enterprise. He has accused the agency's scientists of ignoring vaccine harms to children, comparing it to the Catholic Church's coverup of child sex abuse. He has also disparaged the Covid-19 vaccine, calling it the ''deadliest'' vaccine ever made.\par \par \uc2 Some scientists said the attack was an extreme example of the violence many health workers have experienced since the pandemic began.\par \par \uc2 ''The intersection of disinformation, conspiracy theories and political violence is getting scarier by the day,'' said Dr. Celine Gounder, an infectious disease specialist at \uc2 Bellevue Hospital Center\uc2 . ''I'm very worried about how this is now going beyond defunding of infectious diseases and public health to political violence against the people working in those fields,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 Health care workers make up 10 percent of the nation's work force, but they experience nearly half of the nonfatal injuries incurred, according to 2023 data from the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nearly 9,000 employees and contractors work at the campus where the shooting took place, but it is unclear how many might have been absent because of off-site work and vacations, or because they had just left the office.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Fiona Havers, who resigned from her position as a senior \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  adviser on vaccine policy earlier this year, was on lockdown at \uc2 Emory University Hospital\uc2  while visiting a colleague. She heard the sirens, and stayed in close contact with her friends and former colleagues, including in a 900-person chat group where \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  employees shared terrifying details of the shooting.\par \par \uc2 ''I am feeling very angry and very sad for my colleagues that are still at \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2 ,'' said Dr. Havers, who quit after Mr. Kennedy fired all 17 members of a committee that makes recommendations on which shots Americans should take and when.\par \par \uc2 ''This was a major attack on a federal facility,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250811el8b0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
