\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters and The Associated Press \par \uc2 499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 COMPANIES\par \par \uc2 Peloton to Cut More Jobs As It Forecasts Strong '26\par \par \uc2 Peloton Interactive\uc2  forecast 2026 revenue above estimates and said it would cut 6 percent of its global work force to boost cost savings under an ongoing turnaround effort, sending the exercise-bike maker's shares more than 11 percent higher.\par \par \uc2 The company also posted a surprise fourth-quarter profit on Thursday and said it will ''adjust prices'' to offset the impact of extra costs associated with tariffs.\par \par \uc2 It expects a $65 million hit from tariffs on 2026 free cash flow, the latest U.S. company to brace for uncertainties around how the Trump administration's changing trade policies will affect sourcing, costs and demand.\par \par \uc2 The layoffs, along with plans to cut indirect costs and relocate offices, are expected to help save an additional $100 million by the end of its next fiscal year, Peloton said.\par \par \uc2 The company forecast 2026 revenue between $2.4 billion and $2.5 billion, higher than analysts' estimate of $2.41 billion. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 ENTERTAINMENT\par \par \uc2 Sony\uc2  Lifts Profit Forecast Amid Less Tariff Damage\par \par \uc2 Japanese entertainment and electronics company \uc2 Sony\uc2  said Thursday that its profit surged 23 percent in the last quarter from the year before, as damage from President Trump's tariffs was less than it had expected.\par \par \uc2 The Tokyo-based company reported its April-June profit totaled 259 billion yen, or $1.8 billion, up from 210 billion yen. Quarterly sales edged up 2 percent to 2.6 trillion yen ($17.7 billion) as demand grew for games and services, imaging solutions and sensors.\par \par \uc2 The maker of PlayStation game machines, digital cameras, Walkman audio players and Spider-Man movies said those positive factors offset the negative impact from unfavorable exchange rates. \uc2 Sony\uc2  said it was drawing more subscribers to its online services.\par \par \uc2 Sony\uc2  raised its forecast for its profit in the full fiscal year until March 2026 to 970 billion yen ($6.6 billion), from an earlier forecast of 930 billion yen ($6.3 billion). ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 TECHNOLOGY\par \par \uc2 Surging A.I. Stocks Give \uc2 SoftBank\uc2  Better Outlook\par \par \uc2 Japanese technology conglomerate \uc2 SoftBank Group Corp.\uc2  posted a 421.8 billion yen ($2.9 billion) profit in the April-June quarter, rebounding from a loss a year earlier as its investments benefited from the craze for artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 Quarterly sales at Tokyo-based \uc2 SoftBank Group\uc2 , which invests heavily in A.I. companies like \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  and \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , rose 7 percent to 1.8 trillion yen ($12 billion), the company said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 SoftBank\uc2 's loss in April-June 2024 was 174 billion yen.\par \par \uc2 The company's fortunes tend to fluctuate because it invests in a range of ventures through its Vision Funds, a move with risks.\par \par \uc2 The group's founder \uc2 Masayoshi Son\uc2  sees a vibrant future in A.I.\par \par \uc2 SoftBank\uc2  has also invested in \uc2 Arm Holdings\uc2  and \uc2 Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co.\uc2  Both companies, which produce computer chips, have greatly benefited from the growth of A.I. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250808el880004v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
