\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Google\uc2  Hires Leaders of A.I. Start-Up\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tripp Mickle and Mike Isaac \par \uc2 732 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 In a $2.4 billion deal, \uc2 Google\uc2  recruited the chief executive and a co-founder of Windsurf, which \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  had been in talks to buy, as the battle to dominate artificial intelligence escalates.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  has joined Silicon Valley's scramble to scoop up artificial intelligence engineers, hiring the leaders of Windsurf, a start-up that developed an A.I.-powered computer programming tool, in a $2.4 billion deal.\par \par \uc2 The move, which became public on Friday, was the latest example of how tech companies are waging battles to suck up A.I. talent. The deal deepens \uc2 Google\uc2 's bench of A.I. engineers while also scoring it a point against \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , one of its biggest challengers in the field.\par \par \uc2 In May, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  was in talks to acquire Windsurf in a $3 billion deal that would help add thousands of new customers and expand \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's offerings. But the talks broke down in recent weeks because Windsurf's leaders had concerns about the information it might have to share about its product with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , one of \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's largest investors, two people with knowledge of the deal said.\par \par \uc2 Under \uc2 Google\uc2 's agreement, Varun Mohan, the chief executive of Windsurf, and Douglas Chen, a co-founder, will join \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2 , the company's A.I. division, along with several of Windsurf's research and development employees. \uc2 Google\uc2  is also paying for a nonexclusive license for Windsurf technology.\par \par \uc2 ''We're excited to welcome some top A.I. coding talent from Windsurf's team to \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2  to advance our work in agentic coding,'' \uc2 Google\uc2  said in a statement. As part of the statement, Mr. Mohan and Mr. Chen said they were excited to join \uc2 Google\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Verge and The Information earlier reported on Windsurf's deal.\par \par \uc2 Silicon Valley giants including \uc2 Meta\uc2  have lately poached A.I. talent from rivals and start-ups, sometimes offering compensation packages as high as $100 million. \uc2 Google\uc2  has chosen to pay to bring on top A.I. talent from start-ups rather than acquiring the smaller businesses outright. In 2023, \uc2 Google\uc2  agreed to pay $3 billion to license technology from \uc2 Character.AI\uc2 , a chatbot start-up. The deal allowed \uc2 Google\uc2  to hire Noam Shazeer and Daniel De Freitas, who both had left \uc2 Google\uc2  to start \uc2 Character.ai\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the Biden administration, investments by tech giants in A.I. start-ups drew attention from regulators, who were concerned that the deals were structured to sidestep scrutiny. The Federal Trade Commission and Justice Department review acquisitions to make sure they do not reduce competition, but they typically do not review licensing agreements or hires.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 's window to negotiate with Windsurf opened when talks between the start-up and \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  faltered and a deal exclusivity agreement between the two companies expired, the two people familiar with the conversations said.\par \par \uc2 Complications in those talks arose over some of the terms of \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's agreement with \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , the people said. \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's investment requires \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  to share intellectual property around technology as part of any acquisition. \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  asked for an exception so it would not have to share such data related to Windsurf, but \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  declined to grant one, the people said.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  has made exceptions in the past, including with \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's recent purchase of IO, a hardware device start-up founded by Jony Ive, \uc2 Apple\uc2 's former design chief, the people said. \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  accommodated the IO deal because the company did not see itself in the A.I. hardware consumer device business, the people said.\par \par \uc2 That was not the case with Windsurf, which creates A.I.-powered coding software, a business that \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  competes in with its own product, Copilot.\par \par \uc2 After the exclusivity agreement expired, Windsurf began talking to other companies, the people said. \uc2 Sundar Pichai\uc2 , \uc2 Google\uc2 's chief executive, and Demis Hassabis, who runs DeepMind, offered a straightforward deal with fewer potential issues, the people said.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  spokeswoman confirmed that the company's exclusivity agreement with Windsurf had expired and declined to comment further. A \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  spokesman declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Windsurf said Jeff Wang, its head of business, would become its interim chief executive.\par \par \uc2 (The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  has sued \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , accusing them of copyright infringement regarding news content related to A.I. systems. \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  have denied those claims.)\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250714el7e00030\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
