\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters \par \uc2 473 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 July 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CHEMICALS\par \par \uc2 Dow to Close Three Plants\par \par \uc2 In E.U. and Cut 800 Jobs\par \par \uc2 Dow will shut three upstream plants in Europe and cut around 800 jobs to respond to structural challenges in the region, the chemicals company said Monday.\par \par \uc2 Dow said the shutdowns will remove higher-cost, energy-intensive portions of its portfolio in Europe. Global chemical companies are feeling the pressure to reassess strategies with the increasing production costs, lackluster demand and stringent environmental regulations in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Dow said it had started a review of some of its European assets.\par \par \uc2 An Ethylene cracker in B\u246\'00\'F6hlen, Germany; Chlor-alkali & vinyl assets in Schkopau, Germany; and a Basics siloxanes plant in Barry, U.K. will be shut in the next two years, the company said.\par \par \uc2 The Michigan-based company said the 800 jobs is in addition to the reduction of about 1,500 Dow roles announced in January as part of a $1 billion cost savings plan. Reuters\par \par \uc2 CRYPTOCURRENCY\par \par \uc2 $9 Billion All-Stock Deal Offered for \uc2 Core Scientific\par \par \uc2 CoreWeave\uc2  will buy the crypto miner \uc2 Core Scientific\uc2  in an all-stock deal valued at about $9 billion, it said on Monday, as A.I. infrastructure firms race to secure the energy and data center capacity needed to power demand.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin miners' energy-intensive sites and power contracts, built during the crypto boom, have emerged as prime targets for A.I. companies expanding their computing infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 The deal will help eliminate over $10 billion of cumulative future lease overhead to be paid for existing contractual sites over the next 12 years, \uc2 CoreWeave\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The offer values \uc2 Core Scientific\uc2  at $20.40 per share, a premium of around 66 percent to the stock's closing price before reports surfaced in late June. \uc2 Core Scientific\uc2  stockholders will receive 0.1235 newly issued \uc2 CoreWeave\uc2  stock for each share.\par \par \uc2 The deal is expected to close in the fourth quarter. Reuters\par \par \uc2 MEDIA\par \par \uc2 Trump Media Kicks Off\par \par \uc2 Streaming App Truth+\par \par \uc2 Trump Media & Technology Group\uc2  launched its TV streaming platform, Truth+, globally on Monday, featuring the conservative cable channel \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  to support the company's expansion.\par \par \uc2 The move also allows \uc2 Newsmax\uc2 , which went public in March, to increase its presence outside the United States.\par \par \uc2 Trump Media said users can now access streaming channels and on-demand video through Truth+ apps on iOS, Android, web and connected TV platforms, including \uc2 Apple\uc2  TV, Android TV, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Fire TV and \uc2 Roku\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company, which runs the social media platform Truth Social, began beta testing the global rollout of Truth+ in late June.\par \par \uc2 Trump Media said it would continue to beta test the streaming technology and collect user feedback as the rollout progresses.\par \par \uc2 Shares of Trump Media rose about 0.6 percent, while \uc2 Newsmax\uc2  shares fell 2.6 percent in morning trading. Reuters\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250708el780004i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
