\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  to Lay Off 9,000 Employees, About 4% of Its Work Force\b0\par\par\uc2 By Karen Weise \par \uc2 558 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 July 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The reductions followed cuts of about 6,000 positions last quarter, and were indicative of a tightening job market at big technology companies.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  said on Wednesday that it would lay off roughly 4 percent of its work force, or about 9,000 people, in another indication of the tightening job market at big technology companies.\par \par \uc2 The layoffs follow a reduction of about 6,000 positions in May. \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  had 228,000 employees at the end of June 2024, its most recent disclosure.\par \par \uc2 Though the outlook for the economy has been shaky in recent months, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  has continued to produce multibillion-dollar quarterly profits. Its last earnings report showed unexpected strength, and investors have driven its market valuation up to almost $3.7 trillion. But \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  is in the middle of an expensive investment in artificial intelligence, including spending billions to lease and build data centers to support the demand for cloud computing and A.I.\par \par \uc2 The cuts were also a sign that \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's A.I. development may be having an impact on the size of its own work force. \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's A.I. product for coding and software development, Github Copilot, now has more than 15 million users, and executives have marveled publicly about how effective it has become.\par \par \uc2 Executives at a number of other tech companies have hinted that they expect A.I. to replace some of their workers. \uc2 Andy Jassy\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's chief executive, told employees last month that he expected its corporate work force to shrink in the coming years ''as we get efficiency gains from using A.I. extensively across the company.''\par \par \uc2 The tough outlook for rank and file tech workers stands in contrast to the intense competition for top A.I. researchers. \uc2 Meta\uc2 , for example, has been heavily recruiting top researchers, dangling job offers that on one occasion hit $100 million.\par \par \uc2 (The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  has sued \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and its partner \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , claiming copyright infringement of news content related to A.I. systems. The two companies have denied the suit's claims.)\par \par \uc2 The cuts were widely expected internally, as \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  started its new fiscal year on Tuesday. They span geographies and roles at the company, including teams that work in sales and the company's video game business.\par \par \uc2 ''We continue to implement organizational changes necessary to best position the company and teams for success in a dynamic marketplace,'' the company said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Phil Spencer\uc2 , who leads \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's video game business, said in a note to his division on Wednesday that the cuts were part of ''the discipline to prioritize the strongest opportunities'' and focus on areas with the most potential.\par \par \uc2 Along with other big tech companies, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  executives have been talking in recent months about trying to reduce bureaucracy and having each manager oversee more people.\par \par \uc2 In a call with investors at the end of April, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's finance chief, \uc2 Amy Hood\uc2 , said the company was ''increasing our agility by reducing layers with fewer managers.''\par \par \uc2 Managers were trimmed in the previous round of layoffs, but they were not the primary target. Instead, software engineers and individual product managers bore the brunt of the cuts, according to data from \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's home state of Washington published by The Seattle Times.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250703el730003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
